            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "Measures how far the arms depart from mirror images in the frames where the dancer holds a symmetric pose - hands on hips, arms in a matching gesture. There, the left upper arm and forearm should point as the mirrored right ones do, so every difference is error: to the side, in height, and forward or back, for each segment. Unlike hang_symmetry, which sees only the shared sideways shift of hanging arms, it says something about each arm on its own, at whatever arm position the pose has.\n\nIts loss is for t.optimize, added to elbow_hinge's and hang_symmetry's with +, to learn shadow_mag_correct's weights. Flag the frames by eye from the video.\n\nWHICH ARM IS WRONG:\nSymmetry alone cannot say. Two arms wrong the same way are mirror images too, so learning against symmetry alone can make the pose symmetric by moving the good arm as well - in a real take, both hands lifted off the hips. Pair it with body_contact, which knows where the body is, or choose a reference arm (below) if one arm is known to be right.\n\nSYNTAX:\npose_symmetry\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\ntake in:\nShadow quaternions, (frames, 37 or 20 joints, 4), scalar first. A tensor carrying gradients keeps them.\n\nranges:\nAn option: the frames of the symmetric pose, like 1-827, 15428-15741. Required.\n\nevery:\nAn option: if the take was thinned (t[] ::6), the step, so the ranges still name frames of the full take.\n\nsegments:\nAn option: 'upper arms and forearms' (the default) or 'upper arms'.\n\nreference:\nAn option: 'both arms' (the default) pulls both toward each other; 'left arm' or 'right arm' takes that arm as right and moves only the other toward it.\n\nrobust width:\nAn option, in degrees (4). Misses smaller than this count by their square, larger ones only in proportion - a moment where the dancer breaks the pose pulls little.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nloss:\nOne number for t.optimize; smaller is better.\n\nasymmetry:\nSix numbers in degrees, the left arm minus the mirrored right: upper arm to the side (+ left further out), height (+ left higher), forward (+ left further forward), then the same for the forearm.\n\nframes used:\nHow many frames it read.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\nA made-up take of both arms hanging and swaying together: as mirror images (all 0), then with both turned 15 degrees toward the dancer's right - the left arm in, the right out, so the left reads 30 degrees less far out and lower than the mirrored right.\n\nRELATED:\nbody_contact keeps the hands out of the body and on it where they should touch;\nhang_symmetry measures the shared shift of hanging arms; shadow_mag_correct is the correction. The full setup on a real take is examples/shadow_mag_learning.json.",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 760,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "3": {
                    "name": "height",
                    "value": 1300,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "4": {
                    "name": "text_size",
